TagLib 1.11.1
-------------
The bridge links TagLib revision e36a9cabb9882e61276161c23834d966d62073b7
statically into a separately loaded shared library; the executable itself
loads that bridge dynamically. TagLib's source archive contains COPYING.LGPL
(LGPL-2.1) and COPYING.MPL; consult the applicable upstream terms. Source:
https://github.com/taglib/taglib/archive/e36a9cabb9882e61276161c23834d966d62073b7.tar.gz
SHA-256: 5c80b1e5273849122ef11b5a9116e4b7f182b899cfdb28aefb704087216e1360

The release packaging recipe supplies the unmodified TagLib source archive,
the bridge source and header, the corresponding bridge object and libtag.a,
and complete relinking instructions in corresponding-source/RELINK.txt; it
includes the license texts, rather than relying on a written source offer.
Users may modify TagLib and reverse engineer the application to debug those
modifications, to the extent required by the applicable LGPL terms. Rebuilding
the bridge can change behavior and bytes. On Linux, the shipped CLI refuses a
modified bridge whose digest is not in its architecture-specific allowlist;
using one requires building the public CLI source with an appropriately changed
allowlist as well. That operation is not evidence of parity.

